  "passage": "The train was twenty minutes late. People at the station sighed, checked their phones, and looked at the clock.\nA little boy began counting pigeons on the platform. His mother smiled and joined him. Soon, an old man told them that pigeons often returned to the same station because they remembered places well.\nAnother passenger heard this and shared a story about a bird that flew home from far away. People nearby began listening.\nWhen the train finally arrived, the waiting time no longer felt wasted.\nMost passengers still wished the train had been on time. But some of them left with a new fact, a small story, and a quieter mood. Delay had made strangers talk.",
